  [1mWhat it builds:[0m the page is assembled from the kit components already vendored in [38;5;153mvendor/kit/[39m, so most of the
  behaviour comes from tested code:
  - [38;5;153mpageHeader[39m for the title and snapshot time.
  - [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m and [38;5;153mselectField[39m for the environment dropdown. They keep the current sort in hidden fields, and
    [38;5;153mpublic/kit.js[39m reloads the page when the choice changes.
  - [38;5;153mdataTable[39m for sorting, sort links, [38;5;153maria-sort[39m and the arrows.
  - [38;5;153mbadge[39m for the status chips: ok is green, bad red, warn amber, info blue.
  - [38;5;153memptyState[39m for the empty message.

  The behaviour matches the Services page, but the page doesn't copy its hand-written HTML.

